# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# Sileo, the package manager (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.sileo): the Procursus prefix is grafted onto /var/jb by
# init (tools/mk-jb.sh puts it in the image), so first the preparation the bootstrap wants once per
# boot (the package "firmware" that every other package depends on), then a word from dpkg and apt
# that they run at all, then a package installed from the repository over the network to prove the
# prefix takes one. Then the lock screen is swiped away and Sileo -- a system application here, so
# that LaunchServices finds it by walking /Applications as it does for every other -- is opened;
# "xl screenshot" shows what came of it. At the end, what the user's corner of the prefix holds.
/redwood/bin/sound_test springboard
/var/jb/bin/sh /var/jb/prep.sh
/var/jb/usr/bin/dpkg --version
/var/jb/usr/bin/apt-get --version
/var/jb/usr/bin/dpkg-query -W -f${binary:Package}_${Version}_${Status}\n org.coolstar.sileo firmware
/var/jb/usr/bin/apt-get update
/var/jb/usr/bin/apt-get install -y tree
/var/jb/usr/bin/tree -L 1 /var/jb
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 4 swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 200 wait 8
/var/jb/usr/bin/uiopen sileo://
# its first screen: the notifications it asks for, and the analytics it offers
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 14 tap 0.32 0.59 wait 3 tap 0.5 0.826 wait 25 tap 0.5 0.93 wait 60
/var/jb/usr/bin/find /var/jb/var/mobile -maxdepth 4
